(VAR-53: the bare-identifier character set. LANGUAGE.md:686 gives the set as
 [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*, which admits a leading underscore. The compiler
 rejects a leading underscore as reserved for the runtime — see Discrepancy 9
 — so what this probe records is the set the compiler ACTUALLY accepts: a
 leading letter in either case, digits and underscores after it.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox VAR-53.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   1
   2
   3
)
a number called Total2 is 1.
a number called a_b_9 is 2.
a number called z is 3.
Print Total2.
Print a_b_9.
Print z.
